Implementation State: Executable Foundation Architecture

1. IMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE
The OneDraft persistence and API contract established the system's machine interface and transactional memory.
The next layer converts that contract into an executable software system.
The implementation stack shall therefore provide the runtime required to execute:
CLIENT
    ↓
WEB APPLICATION
    ↓
API
    ↓
AUTHORIZATION
    ↓
DOMAIN SERVICES
    ↓
PROJECT MODEL
    ↓
POSTGRESQL
    ↓
WORK QUEUE
    ↓
WORKERS
    ↓
GEOMETRY
    ↓
VALIDATION
    ↓
DOCUMENTATION
    ↓
OBJECT STORAGE
Aria operates through the same controlled application boundary.
Aria does not become the database.
Aria does not become the project model.
Aria operates the project model through defined domain capabilities.

