77. DATABASE SERVICE ACCOUNT
The API should use a controlled database identity.
Workers should use appropriate restricted credentials.
The frontend receives no database credentials.
No external client receives PostgreSQL access.

78. OBJECT STORAGE SECURITY
Generated project documents must be protected by project authorization.
Object references must not be assumed to constitute authorization.
Downloads should be mediated through controlled access.

79. AUDIT SECURITY
Audit records are append-only.
Normal application users cannot modify historical event records.
Administrative capabilities must themselves produce audit events.

80. IDEMPOTENCY IMPLEMENTATION
Mutating API requests shall support:
Idempotency-Key
The API stores the request identity and resulting response.
A repeated request with the same key and same request hash returns the existing result.
A reused key with a different request hash is rejected.

